cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use vibe-shield in research, teaching, or a product, please cite it as below."
title: "vibe-shield: a security scanner and MCP guard for AI-generated code"
abstract: >-
  vibe-shield is a zero-dependency static security analyzer for code written by
  autonomous coding agents. It detects the vulnerability classes that agents
  ship most often — credentials leaked into client bundles, mutation endpoints
  with no authentication, Postgres tables without Row Level Security,
  SQL injection, unverified webhooks, prompt-injection sinks and poisoned
  agent skills or MCP servers — and reports them with an exact file, line,
  CWE and ordered remediation steps. It ships 91 detection signatures, a
  Model Context Protocol server, SARIF 2.1.0 export for CI code scanning, and
  an Agent Skill that forces an audit before a task is reported complete.
